commit 2c12f80813ada556aaf69dcd9585de9634bb13c7
Author: Ben <gammapod@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Jul 3 20:26:32 2026 -0700

    SadConsole+Blazor+Itch.io spike

diff --git a/docs/Spikes/Html5-SadConsole-Browser-Spike.md b/docs/Spikes/Html5-SadConsole-Browser-Spike.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1d33f12
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/Spikes/Html5-SadConsole-Browser-Spike.md
@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@
+# HTML5 SadConsole Browser Spike
+
+Status: prototype evidence from `html5-spike` branch.
+
+## Outcome
+
+The existing `SadConsoleShell` can run in browser through KNI Blazor/WebGL when SadConsole's MonoGame host is source-built against KNI instead of the published `MonoGame.Framework.DesktopGL` package.
+
+Validated locally:
+
+- browser renders the SadConsole scenario catalog menu with Beta content;
+- 8 Beta scenarios appear in the catalog (from embedded resources);
+- selecting a scenario launches it and the shared Core simulation runs;
+- keyboard input reaches the existing `SadConsoleShell`;
+- Arrow keys advance the shared Core simulation and update logs/panels;
+- static debug publish can be served as an itch.io-style root `index.html` bundle.
+
+Working artifacts from this session:
+
+- `artifacts/GameGameGame-html5-itch.zip` (10.7 MB debug, 28.4 MB uncompressed zip)
+- `tools/build-html5-itch.ps1` — build + package script for itch.io
+
+## itch.io deployment
+
+### Root cause of previous 404 failures
+
+Two issues caused the Blazor WASM loader to fail on itch.io:
+
+1. **Brotli/gzip compression**: itch.io's CDN does not serve `Content-Encoding: br`
+   or `Content-Encoding: gzip` headers for `.br`/`.gz` files. The Blazor loader's
+   `fetch()` calls received the raw compressed bytes without proper encoding
+   headers, causing decompression failures that appeared as 404s in the console.
+   Fixed by stripping `.br`/`.gz` artifacts after publish.
+
+2. **Zip structure flattening**: Using `Compress-Archive` with `Get-ChildItem
+   -Recurse` flattened the directory structure, placing `_framework/`,
+   `_content/`, and `css/` files at the zip root instead of in their proper
+   subdirectories. Fixed by using `System.IO.Compression.ZipFile` API with
+   explicit relative paths.
+
+### itch.io upload procedure
+
+```powershell
+# Build and package for itch.io
+.\tools\build-html5-itch.ps1 -Configuration Debug
+
+# Or just re-zip an existing publish (skip dotnet publish)
+.\tools\build-html5-itch.ps1 -SkipPublish
+
+# Test locally before uploading
+.\tools\build-html5-itch.ps1 -ServeLocal
+```
+
+Upload `artifacts/GameGameGame-html5-itch.zip` to itch.io via the
+HTML Game upload form or Butler CLI.
+
+### Key configuration for itch.io
+
+- `<base href="./" />` in `index.html` — resolves relative paths correctly
+  inside itch.io's iframe/CDN serving. Confirmed by community reports
+  (Faerie Tavern GMTK 2022 devlog).
+- `<BlazorEnableCompression>false</BlazorEnableCompression>` in csproj —
+  prevents `.br`/`.gz` generation (though the build script also strips them
+  defensively).
+- No PWA / service worker — PWA caching in Chrome caused inconsistent
+  loading behavior on itch.io.
+
+## Important caveats
+
+- This is not production-ready dependency wiring. The browser project currently references a local SadConsole source checkout through `$(SadConsoleSourceRoot)`.
+- The published `SadConsole.Host.MonoGame` NuGet package plus `MonoGame.Framework.DesktopGL` compiles in a browser project, but fails at runtime in browser with `TypeInitialization_Type, Keyboard`.
+- KNI's Blazor scripts worked with `net8.0`; the same path under `net10.0` reached a `Module is not defined` JavaScript error.
+- Release static publish still hit the keyboard type-initialization failure during this spike; debug static publish worked. Keep using the debug artifact until the host/source-build and publish configuration are hardened.
+- Beta content YAML files are embedded as assembly resources in `GameGameGame.Content`. The browser builds a catalog from the embedded manifest and loads scenarios from embedded resources via `ScenarioCatalog.DiscoverEmbeddedCatalog()` and `PlayableScenarioLauncher.CreateFromEmbeddedResource()`. Desktop still uses filesystem discovery. If no Beta scenarios are found, the browser falls back to the Alpha smoke scenario.
+
+## Local reproduction notes
+
+1. Clone SadConsole source outside the repo, for example:
+
+   ```powershell
+   git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/Thraka/SadConsole.git C:\Users\Scramble\AppData\Local\Temp\opencode\SadConsole-src
+   ```
+
+2. Patch `SadConsole.Host.MonoGame/SadConsole.Host.MonoGame.csproj` in that checkout:
+   - add `KNI` to `DefineConstants` alongside `MONOGAME`;
+   - replace `MonoGame.Framework.DesktopGL` with KNI packages, especially `nkast.Kni.Platform.Blazor.GL` and the `nkast.Xna.Framework.*` packages used by the browser project.
+
+3. Build, publish, and package for itch.io:
+
+   ```powershell
+   .\tools\build-html5-itch.ps1 -Configuration Debug
+   ```
+
+4. Test locally:
+
+   ```powershell
+   .\tools\build-html5-itch.ps1 -ServeLocal
+   ```
+
+5. Upload `artifacts/GameGameGame-html5-itch.zip` to itch.io.
+
+## Recommended next hardening
+
+1. Decide whether to vendor a tiny patched SadConsole host project, maintain a fork/package, or upstream a first-class KNI host package.
+2. ~~Add a browser-safe scenario catalog/launch path over bundled content, reusing `PlayableScenarioLauncher` semantics.~~ Done: Beta scenarios load from embedded resources.
+3. Identify why Release static publish regresses and pin linker/trimming/reflection settings.
+4. Add an automated Playwright smoke that waits for the SadConsole canvas, presses one movement key, and verifies no browser page errors.
+5. Verify the itch.io upload actually loads and runs in browser with the Beta scenario catalog.
